title: Recalled
subtitle: Member worlds turn on their Caucus senators.
tags: event
view-if: recall_ready and not finale and not game_ending
priority: 3
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_rim.svg

= Recalled

Member worlds across the [+ recall_region_name +] are recalling their Caucus senators, furious at [+ recall_why +]. The worlds' new delegations will sit with other blocs.

*A region's grievance builds when the Caucus backs measures that hurt it, such as a levy on the Core, a debased credit, cuts to Rim relief, tariffs, or budgets that starve a war. It fades with time. The Polls tab shows which regions are aggrieved.*

- @apologise: Apologise, and promise to make it right.
- @campaign: Fight to hold the seats.
- @accept: Accept the losses.

@apologise
subtitle: −1 political capital. Fewer seats lost, and the grievance is cleared. The Institutionalists wince.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {! SW.recallResolve(Q, 'apologise'); Q.inst_dissent += 2; !}

The Caucus's leaders tour the [+ recall_region_name +], listening more than talking. Some worlds keep their Caucus senators. We still lose about [+ recall_lost +] points of support there.

@campaign
subtitle: −1 political capital. Fewer seats lost, and local allies remember the fight.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {! SW.recallResolve(Q, 'campaign'); !}

The Caucus fights recall by recall. We lose about [+ recall_lost +] points of support in the [+ recall_region_name +], less than we feared.

@accept
subtitle: No cost now, and the heaviest losses.
on-arrival: {! SW.recallResolve(Q, 'accept'); !}

The recalls go through. The Caucus loses about [+ recall_lost +] points of support in the [+ recall_region_name +].
